<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lorenzo de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1449">1449</a>–<a href="/years/1492">1492</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lorenzo the Magnificent</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lorenzo de' Medici, called the Magnificent, was the effective ruler of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> from 1469 until his death. He survived the Pazzi conspiracy of 1478, in which his brother Giuliano was killed, and worked to keep peace among the Italian states through diplomacy. A poet and a patron of artists such as Botticelli and the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>, he came to embody the Florentine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici.jpg" alt="Lorenzo de' Medici" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Bronzino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lorenzo_de_Medici.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
